; the program: Chrome's window -- the tabs, the omnibox, the
; developer tools -- around the tabs of src/chrome (MiniChrome.ml).
;
; Drawn by the Playground, on one of its native platforms, SDL for the
; window either way: Cairo's (elm_playground_native) or its own
; rasterizer (elm_playground_software). The platform is a virtual
; library, one implementation linked into an executable, so the choice
; is made when linking: mini-chrome takes Cairo's when it is installed,
; else the software one (the select below, which links the libraries of
; the first alternative available; Platform_choice says which), and
; software/'s mini-chrome-software is always the software one.
; ./configure --software, or no Cairo, leaves elm_playground_native out.
(executable
 (name MiniChrome)
 (public_name mini-chrome)
 (flags (:standard -open Network)) ; ours, not the Playground's (libs/network/dune)
 (libraries
   caps ; the authority to reach the network, and the profile's files
   logs ; a profile that cannot be read, said
   mini_opti ; opti=off
   tiny_libs.core network
   mini_gui ; Gui_text, Gui_menu
   lang_html lang_css browser_layout
   browser_url browser_display browser_www browser_viewers browser_about browser_chrome
   browser_window ; the program: its model, update and view
   elm_playground
   (select Platform_choice.ml from
     (elm_playground_native -> Platform_choice.cairo.ml) ; SDL and Cairo
     (elm_playground_software -> Platform_choice.software.ml)))) ; SDL and our own rasterizer
